# XSH getgrent(), setgrent(), endgrent()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# All three are XSI (shaded in the synopsis). The database may hide entries, so nothing about its size or
# content is assumed beyond: an entry the caller can look up exists, and iteration is consistent with it.

assertion  XSH.getgrent.001
anchor     functions/getgrent.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getgrent.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       After setgrent(), repeated getgrent() calls return entries, each with
           a name, and finally a null pointer with errno unchanged (errno is set
           just before the call that ends it).
note       At least one entry must be visible, else UNRESOLVED (the page lets the
           system hide entries).
test       t/001-iterate.c

assertion  XSH.getgrent.002
anchor     functions/getgrent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       Reading the entire group database with getgrent() visits the entry
           that getgrgid() finds for the caller (same name and group ID).
note       The page lets a system hide entries of other users and groups, not the
           caller's own.
test       t/002-own.c

assertion  XSH.getgrent.003
anchor     functions/getgrent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       setgrent() makes the next getgrent() return the first entry again:
           after one or two reads, and after reading up to the end.
test       t/003-rewind.c

assertion  XSH.getgrent.004
anchor     functions/getgrent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       After endgrent() the next getgrent() opens the database again and
           returns the first entry; endgrent() followed by setgrent() does the
           same.
test       t/004-end.c

assertion  XSH.getgrent.005
anchor     functions/getgrent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       setgrent() and endgrent() do not change errno when they succeed (open
           or closed database).
note       A change to one of the listed errors is a failure of the call and
           gives UNRESOLVED.
test       t/005-errno.c

assertion  XSH.getgrent.006
anchor     functions/getgrent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       The names of the first entries read with getgrent() are each found by
           getgrnam().
test       t/006-lookup.c
